@startuml 03_state_scheduler
title Scheduler state machine\n(src/scheduler/scheduler.cpp, button handling in src/main.cpp)
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #DAE8FC
  BorderColor #6C8EBF
  BackgroundColor<<error>> #F8CECC
  BorderColor<<error>> #B85450
}

[*] --> WAITING : setup() ends with triggerStop()

state WAITING : nothing is driven
state CHECK_CONNECT : GRBL, RFID and servo\nare probed\n(Dolibarr check disabled)
state INIT_POSITIONS : placeholder steps
state PRODUCTION : conveyor moves forward every tick\nsorter.production() runs every tick
state ERROR <<error>> : conveyor stopped\ncritical error may be latched

WAITING --> CHECK_CONNECT : Button A
CHECK_CONNECT --> INIT_POSITIONS : checkConnections() OK
CHECK_CONNECT --> WAITING : a check fails
INIT_POSITIONS --> PRODUCTION : initializePositions() OK
INIT_POSITIONS --> WAITING : initialization fails
PRODUCTION --> WAITING : Button B (triggerStop)
PRODUCTION --> WAITING : conveyor is ALARM\n(guard in executeCurrentState)
PRODUCTION --> ERROR : conveyor ALARM\n(state rules CRITICAL + FATAL)
ERROR --> WAITING : auto recovery\n[no latched critical error\n and connections OK]
ERROR --> CHECK_CONNECT : Button A\n(clears the latched critical error first)

note right of ERROR
  Automatic recovery never clears a
  latched critical error. Only Button A
  does, from ERROR or WAITING.
end note
@enduml
